Z||000000||cmyokley||09-17-1999||05:48 PM||||I want to put some aftermarket 16-17 wheels on my 86GT with lower profile tires, say P225 to P245 40 series. I know the design needs to be 100MM bolt patern with 35MM positive offset.<P>Does anyone have links to sites that offer designs like the Ponitac Firebird 5 spoke High Polish design.<P>Does anyone know what the bolt diameter and offset is for the Pontiac Firebird or Grand Prix/Grand Am?<P>If any of the newer Pontiac wheels will work does anyone have an outlet for used parts?<P>What brand of wheels have worked for those out there that have gone aftermarket?<P>Thanks||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||09-17-1999||10:33 PM||||use of wider wheels will usually require a change in offset.<P>the wider wheel usually want to be pushed out or they won't clear. especially up front.<P>an important number to work out is the "Total Backset." This is the backset of the mounted tire, not just the rim. If you change radius of the tire, backset is even more critical up front as a larger diameter tire will contact the inner fender sooner.||||reg||1
